framework DecisionAudit

domain PlanReviewByteLimit:
  description "Resume public contract WIP at e39c739f"

problem P1:
  "Reject oversized direct-library composed batch input before canonical string allocation"

step S1:
  premise PR1:
    "User requests resumption from latest handoff; accepted spec section 10 bounds composed JSON to 8388608 UTF-8 bytes before allocation or expansion"

step S2:
  evidence EV1:
    "request.ts normalizedBatch currently calls rfc8785Json before checking encoded length"
    resource:
      file "src/plan-review/request.ts"
      label "Observed allocation order"

step S3:
  evidence EV2:
    "model/rfc8785.ts serializes strings with JSON escaping and permits safe integers, arrays and objects"
    resource:
      file "src/model/rfc8785.ts"
      label "Canonical serializer semantics"

step S4:
  decision I1 based_on PR1, EV1, EV2:
    "A bounded counting pass can reject oversize without materializing escaped strings or full JSON while retaining exact accepted canonical identity"

step S5:
  premise A1:
    "Checking only source string lengths undercounts escaping and multibyte UTF-8"

step S6:
  decision D1 based_on P1, A1, PR1, EV1, EV2, I1:
    "Add an internal Plan Review byte counter for canonical JSON syntax, string escapes, Unicode and safe integers; stop at the limit, then call existing canonicalizer only for bounded input; verify exact boundary and early rejection through direct library APIs"

step S7:
  pending PD1:
    "Full closed-case acceptance belongs to PLAN_REVIEW_ACCEPTANCE; owner acceptance, PERT mutation, push, merge and release remain separate. Invalid object graphs must fail closed. No external beneficiary release occurs in this correction."

step S8:
  evidence EV3:
    "Final bounded full-suite run exited zero with 1396 tests; static, English, docs, self-use, isolated LSP/MCP, supported VSIX, link and public-package gates passed"
    resource:
      file "test/plan-review-request-size.test.mjs"
      label "Direct-library preallocation regression"

step S9:
  evidence EV4:
    "The handoff keeps PLAN_REVIEW_PUBLIC_CONTRACT planned until the direct-library gap and complete gate are resolved. The status-only done preview changes one task status, has no affected governance scope or owner assertion, and reports write_authorized true"
    resource:
      file "docs/process/plan-review-public-contract-wip-handoff-2026-09-29.md"
      label "Task completion boundary"

step S10:
  decision D2 based_on P1, PR1, EV3, EV4, D1:
    "Record only PLAN_REVIEW_PUBLIC_CONTRACT technical completion with actor codex and the preview source digest; read back check, both schedules and Next. Owner acceptance, receipts, outcomes, advance, remote writes and releases remain separate"
